WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:03.170
- In a world full of Zoom calls

00:00:03.170 --> 00:00:05.770
when people can only see our top half,

00:00:05.770 --> 00:00:07.240
Winnie the Pooh style,

00:00:07.240 --> 00:00:09.520
how can we still be glamorous

00:00:09.520 --> 00:00:13.330
while sitting at home on our
couches or working from home?

00:00:13.330 --> 00:00:16.230
Well, our next guest has that answer.

00:00:16.230 --> 00:00:20.880
He has designed some of
the most iconic gowns ever

00:00:20.880 --> 00:00:22.280
and he's one of my favorite people,

00:00:22.280 --> 00:00:24.430
let alone mentors on "Project Runway."

00:00:24.430 --> 00:00:27.004
Please welcome Christian Siriano.

00:00:27.004 --> 00:00:30.770
(upbeat music)
(audience cheers)

00:00:30.770 --> 00:00:32.769
- You look divine.

00:00:32.769 --> 00:00:34.710
- I do you, you think so?
- You look divine.

00:00:34.710 --> 00:00:35.543
- Thank you.

00:00:36.540 --> 00:00:41.540
Okay, so how did the quarantine affect you

00:00:41.550 --> 00:00:44.170
because when people could
not get their hands on masks,

00:00:44.170 --> 00:00:46.870
there you were at your atelier,

00:00:46.870 --> 00:00:48.060
making it with everyone

00:00:48.060 --> 00:00:51.330
and Cuomo deemed your
business an essential business

00:00:51.330 --> 00:00:53.100
so they could make PPE and open.

00:00:53.100 --> 00:00:54.610
- I tweeted him, I begged him.

00:00:54.610 --> 00:00:55.970
I was like, we wanna help,

00:00:55.970 --> 00:00:57.200
so I was tryin' to keep

00:00:57.200 --> 00:00:59.040
my kind of small business in New York,

00:00:59.040 --> 00:01:00.680
but then also do something great.

00:01:00.680 --> 00:01:02.950
So it all worked out for everybody.

00:01:02.950 --> 00:01:05.703
I will say masks are quite a challenge.

00:01:06.858 --> 00:01:08.730
We've donated almost a million.

00:01:08.730 --> 00:01:11.430
- Wow, everything you're
doing, I admire, I applaud

00:01:11.430 --> 00:01:12.850
and I already loved you,

00:01:12.850 --> 00:01:16.270
but that just put you into
superhero stratosphere.

00:01:16.270 --> 00:01:20.260
Now can we do a little
quarantine fashion show?

00:01:20.260 --> 00:01:21.093
- Yeah.

00:01:21.093 --> 00:01:22.580
- [Drew] What should we do?
Should we bring out Jennifer?

00:01:22.580 --> 00:01:24.430
- Let's bring first look.

00:01:24.430 --> 00:01:25.263
Come on.

00:01:26.789 --> 00:01:27.930
(Drew laughs)

00:01:27.930 --> 00:01:31.910
- This is all about, this
is like no fear have fun,

00:01:31.910 --> 00:01:33.950
kind of like sexy pajamas on bottom

00:01:33.950 --> 00:01:35.690
and then like some glamor on the top.

00:01:35.690 --> 00:01:38.040
- [Drew] It's a little
Samantha Jones on the bottom.

00:01:38.040 --> 00:01:39.540
- [Christian] Samantha
Jones on the bottom.

00:01:39.540 --> 00:01:42.990
- But it's giving me Betsy
Johnson vibes on the top.

00:01:42.990 --> 00:01:45.740
- Old school, I love a dangle earring.

00:01:45.740 --> 00:01:47.730
I wish earrings were all at the shoulder.

00:01:47.730 --> 00:01:51.330
I think that's just like
a hit and headbands,

00:01:51.330 --> 00:01:52.520
I don't always love them,

00:01:52.520 --> 00:01:54.670
but I think for a Zoom call, why not?

00:01:54.670 --> 00:01:57.610
- I have to say, I think you
look absolutely beautiful,

00:01:57.610 --> 00:01:59.123
Jennifer, really.

00:02:00.030 --> 00:02:01.500
- Hair and makeup, a pink lip.

00:02:01.500 --> 00:02:04.580
Why not a pink lip at 10:00
AM for your friends on Zoom?

00:02:04.580 --> 00:02:06.700
- I know. I was hoping my
friends were having a cocktail

00:02:06.700 --> 00:02:08.010
at 9:00 AM on premiere day.

00:02:08.010 --> 00:02:09.360
I was like, is that weird?

00:02:09.360 --> 00:02:11.330
So I a hundred percent, but you're right.

00:02:11.330 --> 00:02:14.430
Accessories make such a huge difference.

00:02:14.430 --> 00:02:16.900
Now, why did you need an outfit, Jennifer?

00:02:16.900 --> 00:02:19.340
- Well, so many people
nowadays are working at home

00:02:19.340 --> 00:02:22.350
and they're doing trainings
and meetings with their bosses

00:02:22.350 --> 00:02:23.750
and clients online,

00:02:23.750 --> 00:02:26.370
so you still have to look good
at least from the waist up

00:02:26.370 --> 00:02:28.100
'cause you can't be going
on with your employer

00:02:28.100 --> 00:02:30.770
with bun in your hair and sweatpants on.

00:02:30.770 --> 00:02:32.075
- I gotta tell you,

00:02:32.075 --> 00:02:32.910
you look like you're straight off holiday.

00:02:32.910 --> 00:02:35.349
Thank you, Jennifer. Seriously.

00:02:35.349 --> 00:02:36.342
- You look gorgeous.

00:02:36.342 --> 00:02:38.070
- Okay, Peyton, will
you please come on out?

00:02:38.070 --> 00:02:40.160
- Okay, I love this look.

00:02:40.160 --> 00:02:41.882
- [Drew] Peyton, are those my shoes?

00:02:41.882 --> 00:02:42.930
- They probably are.

00:02:42.930 --> 00:02:44.990
- I'm not kidding. I
wore those to work today.

00:02:44.990 --> 00:02:46.090
I'm pretty sure.

00:02:46.090 --> 00:02:48.420
By the way I was so
obsessed with the bottom

00:02:48.420 --> 00:02:51.900
because of course I'm like, oh,
moccasins with like a faux--

00:02:51.900 --> 00:02:55.350
- That is not the look.
We're not looking at that.

00:02:55.350 --> 00:02:56.183
Waist up.

00:02:56.183 --> 00:02:57.420
- I know, but of course that's
what I'm gravitating towards,

00:02:57.420 --> 00:03:02.310
but now my eyes raised
and you are all class.

00:03:02.310 --> 00:03:04.890
Now, why did you need an outfit?

00:03:04.890 --> 00:03:07.530
- Well, I'm violently single, Drew,

00:03:07.530 --> 00:03:11.460
so I am using this for a speed
dating online through Zoom.

00:03:11.460 --> 00:03:14.610
- The guys at home are really
struggling. I feel you.

00:03:14.610 --> 00:03:17.840
And the thing is, I think it's
more of a conversation here.

00:03:17.840 --> 00:03:21.130
We have plaids and I don't know
gingham and the whole look.

00:03:21.130 --> 00:03:22.120
It's the vest.

00:03:22.120 --> 00:03:23.120
- Well, I have to say,

00:03:23.120 --> 00:03:27.957
I do miss the era of
bowler hats and jackets

00:03:28.900 --> 00:03:33.500
and a little bit of a more
etiquette style to our fashion.

00:03:33.500 --> 00:03:34.680
- Dress to impress.

00:03:34.680 --> 00:03:37.030
- [Drew] So I think
that you look fantastic.

00:03:37.030 --> 00:03:39.182
- Speed date away.

00:03:39.182 --> 00:03:41.232
- Therese, will you please come out here?

00:03:42.680 --> 00:03:44.720
Oh my god.

00:03:44.720 --> 00:03:48.360
Again, Christian, why am I
going straight to the bottom?

00:03:48.360 --> 00:03:52.370
- No, that is not how you
want to live your life,

00:03:52.370 --> 00:03:54.210
but look, look how comfortable,

00:03:54.210 --> 00:03:55.710
but how glamorous on top.

00:03:55.710 --> 00:03:59.110
Volume and texture, hoops. I love it all.

00:03:59.110 --> 00:04:00.170
- Christian, you have a tip,

00:04:00.170 --> 00:04:02.790
like don't wear soft fabrics

00:04:02.790 --> 00:04:05.010
and maybe go for a little
more tailored on a Zoom look?

00:04:05.010 --> 00:04:07.930
- I just think because
you're in this small screen,

00:04:07.930 --> 00:04:09.620
it's like, you don't want too much,

00:04:09.620 --> 00:04:11.960
it's like much is about
like where's the texture,

00:04:11.960 --> 00:04:13.070
where's the glamor.

00:04:13.070 --> 00:04:15.410
If it's chiffon and
wrinkly, it's not working.

00:04:15.410 --> 00:04:17.990
- I have to say, I am so inspired

00:04:17.990 --> 00:04:20.250
because I get to dress up at work.

00:04:20.250 --> 00:04:23.610
I'm even extra lazy in my real life.

00:04:23.610 --> 00:04:26.840
I'm always in a really threadbare,

00:04:26.840 --> 00:04:28.900
old vintage cotton. T-shirt,

00:04:28.900 --> 00:04:31.410
so now that I'm gonna
step up my home game.

00:04:31.410 --> 00:04:33.960
Now, Therese, why did you need an outfit?

00:04:33.960 --> 00:04:37.360
- Well, I'm wearing this for a
good friend's birthday party,

00:04:37.360 --> 00:04:39.600
so we're sharing recipes, cocktails,

00:04:39.600 --> 00:04:43.140
and the best part is, I don't
have to wear heels or drive.

00:04:43.140 --> 00:04:45.661
- And is it at night or is it a day?

00:04:45.661 --> 00:04:46.494
- It's at night.

00:04:46.494 --> 00:04:48.260
- Uh huh, okay, I think
that changes the game.

00:04:48.260 --> 00:04:50.163
- Yeah, this is an evening look.

00:04:51.085 --> 00:04:54.140
- I love being in your
world in your clothes.

00:04:54.140 --> 00:04:55.110
- I'm in your world.

00:04:55.110 --> 00:04:57.210
- Finally 'cause I've
been living in your world

00:04:57.210 --> 00:05:00.430
and I wanna do so many
things with you, Christian.

00:05:00.430 --> 00:05:04.470
You guys thank you so much,
Jennifer, Peyton, Therese.

00:05:04.470 --> 00:05:07.300
Thank you to our beautiful
quarantined fashion models.

00:05:07.300 --> 00:05:11.347
You are bringing it and
Christian, I love you.

00:05:11.347 --> 00:05:12.830
(audience cheers)

00:05:12.830 --> 00:05:13.980
- Love you.

00:05:13.980 --> 00:05:16.647
(upbeat music)

